6066               /We now determine how justification is to be done.  Justification is done by
6067               /increasing or decreasing inter-position and space sizes.  The options, in
6068               /their order of consideration, are:
6069               
6070               /1.  The line is longer than its desired length.
6071               /       Position spacing is decreased in decrements of one until the resulting
6072               /       line length is less than or equal to the justified length.  We then
6073               /       consider the other options.
6074               
6075               /2.  The line is equal to its justified length.
6076               /       We need do no more and continue with printing the line.
6077               
6078               /If we reach this point in the option list, the line is shorter than its
6079               /desired length.
6080               
6081               /3.  There are no justifiable spaces.
6082               /       Justification is effected solely by increasing the size of
6083               /       inter-position spacing.
6084               
6085               /4.  Each justifiable space can be doubled in size.
6086               /       Justification is effected solely by increasing the size of spaces.
6087               /       This is done because the line is grossly out of justification.
6088               
6089               /5.  Each position width can be increased by one unit.
6090               /       This is done. if the line is too short we continue
6091               /       with option 6
6092               
6093               /6.  Justification remains to be done
6094               /       justification is effected soley by increasing the size of spaces
6095               
6096               / The ammount by which each inter position space is to be increased is
6097               /indicated in PLPS; the ammount by which each space is to be increased is
6098               /indicated in PLSS. Note that the numbers do not always come
6099               /out even, and some spaces must be increased by one unit more than others.
6100               /The positions or spaces suceptible to this increase are indicated by
6101               /setting bit one of the corresponding character
6102               
6103               /PRRM, which is in the ac is the desired right margin.
6104               
6105 030336* 7041          CIA             / subtract the desired line length
6106 030337* 1000          TAD     PRRCH   / from the current line length
