6730               /PRLMOD processes the mode bits which are passed to it in the AC upon
6731               /invocation.  It makes a normal return if the mode bits indicate that the
6732               /character should not print during this pass, and makes a skip return
6733               /otherwise.  The mode bits considered by this routine are in AC2,3,4 at the
6734               /time of call:
6735               
6736               /AC 2 3
6737               /   0 0         print normally
6738               /   0 1         print with underscore
6739               /   1 0         print superscripted
6740               /   1 1         print subscripted
6741               
6742               /AC 4
6743               /   0           not boldface
6744               /   1           boldface
6745               
6746               
6747               PRLMOD,
6748                       XX
undefined       	 ^
     031000* 0000  
6749               
6750               /It is not necessary to give the mode bits the full treatment each time--we
6751               /need only do that every time they change.  The location PRLSWT is patched
6752               /with a jump to the section of the routine appropriate for the mode bits
6753               /should they not change.  First, we determine whether the mode bits have
6754               /indeed changed.  We take the patched jump if they haven't; otherwise, we
6755               /give them the full treatment.
6756               
6757               /Notice that if we are called with AC=7777, this will be treated as a new
6758               /set of bits which don't belong to any pass.  The net effect is to complete
6759               /any pending underlining and reset some variables.  This trick is used when
6760               /finishing a pass and wishing to reset for the next one.
6761               
6762 031001* 7041          CIA             /Negate the mode bits
6763 031002* 1300          TAD     PRLMDB  /Compare with the old ones
6764 031003* 7450          SNA
6765               
6766               PRLSWT,
6767                       XX              /The mode bits haven't changed since last time, so
undefined       	 ^
     031004* 0000  
6768                                       /we can take this jump which was patched with a jump
6769                                       /to the section appropriate to this type of bits.
6770               
6771               /The mode bits have changed.  We recover the new bits, save them, and proceed
6772               /to deal with them.
6773               
6774 031005* 7041          CIA             /Recover the new bits
6775 031006* 1300          TAD     PRLMDB
6776 031007* 3300          DCA     PRLMDB  /And save them
6777               
6778               /If the underline flag is set, we invoke PRUNDL to perform accumulated
6779               /underlining.  Notice that the net effect is that underlining is performed
6780               /in spurts when the mode changes.
6781               
6782 031010* 1301          TAD     PRUFLG  /Check the underlining flag
6783 031011* 7640          SZA CLA
6784 031012* 4777          JMS     PRUNDL  /Do underlining if necessary
6785 031013* 3301          DCA     PRUFLG  /Clear the flag
6786               
6787               /Now, we determine whether or not the current character belongs to this pass.
6788               /We branch accordingly.
6789               
6790 031014* 1300          TAD     PRLMDB  /Get the mode bits
6791 031015* 7102          CLL BSW         /And move them into the lower two bits of the AC
6792 031016* 7012          RTR
6793 031017* 1376          TAD     (-2)    /After these manipulations...
6794 031020* 7540          SMA SZA
6795                       AC7775
undefined       	     ^
     031021* 0000  
6796               
6797               /...the AC has the following values...
6798               
6799               /AC=0           superscript
6800               /AC=-1          underline
6801               /AC=-2          normal
6802               /AC=-3          subscript
6803               
6804               /...while PRPASS, which identifies the current pass, has these values...
6805               
6806               /PRPASS=0       superscript
6807               /PRPASS=1       underline
6808               /PRPASS=2       normal
6809               /PRPASS=3       subscript
6810               
6811               /...so we need only compare the two values.
6812               
6813 031022* 1054          TAD     PRPASS  /Are we in the right pass?
6814 031023* 7640          SZA CLA
6815 031024* 5262          JMP     PRLMO4  /No--jump to handle it
6816               
6817               /We are in the right pass.  The first we must do is set the hit count.  We
6818               /begin by putting the bold bit into the link.
6819               
6820 031025* 1300          TAD     PRLMDB  /Get the mode bits
6821 031026* 7002          BSW             /And put the bold bit into the link
6822 031027* 7012          RTR
6823 031030* 7200          CLA
6824               
6825               /We must concern ourselves with three values:
6826               /1.  The bold bit (now in the link)
6827               /2.  The two wheel flag (PRQ2W)
6828               /3.  The darkness value (PRQOVP)
6829               
6830               /If two-wheel printing is specified, the bold bit takes on a different
6831               /significance.
6832               
6833 031031* 1775          TAD     PRQ2W   /Get the two wheel flag
6834 031032* 7450          SNA             /If AC=0, no two-wheel
6835 031033* 5241          JMP     PRLMO1  /Jump to handle regular printing
6836               
6837               /This section deals with two-wheel printing.
6838               /If PRQ2W is negative, this is the first pass.  Only non-bold text is printed,
6839               /       with a hit count equal to the darkness value.
6840               /If PRQ2W is positive, this is the second pass.  Only bold text is printed,
6841               /       with a hit count equal to the darkness value.
6842               /If text is not to be printed, the hit count is set negative.
6843               
6844 031034* 7700          SMA CLA
6845               
6846               /If this is the first pass, the skip occurs.  In this pass, we want to print
6847               /only the non-bold text; i.e., print only if the link is clear.  If this is
6848               /the second pass, the skip does not occur.  In thispass, we want to print
6849               /only the bold text; i.e., print only if the link is set.
6850               
6851               /Now, if this is the second pass and we complement the link, we will want to
6852               /print then only if the link is clear and the two cases become identical.
6853                       
6854 031035* 7020          CML             /Second pass--complement the link and the two cases
6855                                       /become identical.
6856               
6857               /Now we print only if the link is clear.
6858               
6859 031036* 7430          SZL             /Skip if we need to print during this two-wheel pass
6860                       AC7777          /Otherwise, get a -1 into the AC
undefined       	     ^
