6880               PRLMO1,
6881 031041* 7004          RAL             /Get the hit count                              /M019
6882 031042* 1774          TAD     PRQOVP  /Add in the darkness value
6883               
6884 031043* 4773          JMS     PRESCS  /And send it
6885 031044* 0104                  PCBOLD
6886 031045* 7200                  CLA
6887               
6888               /This is the point to which the routine branches if the mode bits haven't
6889               /changed and the last mode bits indicated the character belonged to the
6890               /current pass.  The first thing which is always done for the proper pass
6891               /is to perform any spacing which has accumulated while characters which were
6892               /not in this pass were printing.  There are several things to note about
6893               /the variables which record this motion:
6894               
6895               /PLOLNC is the amount that accumulated on the last character only.  It is
6896               /       kept separate because these accumualted spacing variables are used
6897               /       in underlining also, and when underlining we do not want to underline
6898               /       the most recent character.
6899               
6900               /PLASPC is the amount that has accumulated on all previous characters.
6901               
6902               /When a backspace is encountered, the current position size PLPOS is
6903               /       subtracted from PLOLNC.  If we were in the wrong pass, it is as if
6904               /       no spacing had ever been included in PLOLNC; if we are in the wrong
6905               /       pass, a backspace is performed the next time this section is reached.
6906               
6907               /This branch is not used for characters which belong to the underlining pass;
6908               /       rather, the spacing is allowed to accumulate and it is performed all
6909               /       at once when an underline is produced.
6910               
6911               PRLMO2,
6912 031046* 1056          TAD     PLOLNC  /We want to move this distance in addition to the
6913                                       /distance in PLASPC which PLHMOV will perform
6914                                       /automatically
6915 031047* 4302          JMS     PLHMOV  /Do the spacing
6916 031050* 3056          DCA     PLOLNC  /PLHMOV clears PLASPC automatically; we also want
6917                                       /to clear this value to indicate the motion has
6918                                       /been performed
6919               
6920               /As noted above, if we are printing the underline pass, we make believe we
6921               /are not printing and merely accumulate space.  When the mode changes again,
6922               /the underlining will be performed as above.
6923               
6924                       AC7777
