     031253* 1000  
8173               
8174               /The largest width found so far in the position is in the AC.  This was
8175               /determined either by comparison (in the proportional case) or because
8176               /all widths are the same (in the non-proportional case).  In either case,
8177               /update PLWIDT.
8178               
8179               PLWID3,
8180 031254* 3270          DCA     PLWIDT  /Record the current largest width
8181 031255* 3062          DCA     PLWMUL  / CLEAR THE MULTINATIONAL FLAG                  /A274
8182               
8183               /We now determine whether the character sequence continues.  If it does,
8184               /we iterate.  If not, we return the width of the position--making a regular
8185               /return if this position is the last position, making a skip return otherwise.
8186               
8187               PLWID4,
8188 031256* 4772          JMS     PLCHBS  /Are there more characters?
8189 031257* 5601          JMP I   PLWIDE  /No--make a regular return
8190 031260* 5263          JMP     PLWD4   /YES, A multinational PRECEDENCE                /a271
8191 031261* 5263          JMP     PLWD4   /YES, A TECHNICAL PRECEDENCE                    /A233
8192 031262* 5203          JMP     PLWID0  /Yes, in this position--iterate
8193               
8194               /The end of the position's character sequence has been found.  Make a skip
8195               /return.
8196               PLWD4,
8197 031263* 2201          ISZ     PLWIDE  /This is not the last position--make a skip return
8198 031264* 5601          JMP I   PLWIDE
8199               
8200               
8201 031265* 1371  PLWR1,  TAD     (37-177)                /USE TABLE PSN BEFORE SPACE     /A218
8202                                                       /FOR R1                         /A218
8203               PLWR2,  TAD     P177                    /USE TABLE PSN 177 FOR R2       /A218
undefined             	   	   ^
undefined             	   	   ^
     031266* 1000  
8204 031267* 5224          JMP     PLWID5                  /RE-ENTER ROUTINE ABOVE         /A218
8205               
8206 031270* 0000  PLWIDT, 0       /The width of the position pointed to by the buffer variables
8207                               /when PLWIDE is invoked.  The return value of the routine.
8208               
8209 031271* 0000  PLWTM,  0       /THE CHARACTER VALUE USED TO INDEX THE TABLE            /A218
