8454               
8455               /THIS OVERLAY IS USED FOR MATRIX PRINTERS AND DD HOST
8456               
8457               /THIS OVERLAY IS RESPONSIBLE FOR JUSTIFYING (IF NECESSARY) AND PRINTING
8458               /THE LINE OF TEXT WHICH HAS BEEN ASSEMBLED IN PRLBUF BY PRGTLN
8459               /EXTERNAL ARGUMENT USED BY JUSTIFICATION OVERLAYS:
8460               
8461               /PLPTR - A POINTER INTO THE LINE BUFFER.  INITIALLY, IT POINTS AT THE LAST
8462               /         CHARACTER IN THE LINE, WHICH IS THE RETURN.
8463               
8464               /PRLBUF - A LITERAL WHICH IS THE ADDRESS OF THE BEGINNING OF THE BUFFER; IT
8465               /         IS THE ADDRESS AT WHICH THE FIRST CHARACTER IS STORED.
8466               
8467               /PRQPIT - THE PITCH VALUE.  IT IS ZERO IF PROPORTIONAL PITCH IS SPECIFIED,
8468               /         NON-ZERO OTHERWISE.
8469               
8470               /PRRM   - THE JUSTIFICATION FLAG.  IT IS ZERO IF THE LINE IS NOT TO BE
8471               /         JUSTIFIED; OTHERWISE, IT THE LENGTH OF THE LINE IN PRINT UNITS.
8472               
8473               /PLNRCS - CHARACTER SIZE.  IT IS THE SIZE OF A CHARACTER IN PRINT UNITS.
8474               
8475               /PRCCH  - PRINT HEAD POSITION.  INITIALLY, IT IS THE POSITION THE PRINT
8476               /         HEAD IS IN.
8477               
8478               /SOME DEFINITIONS WILL MAKE THE COMMENTS EASIER TO FOLLOW:
8479               
8480               /CHARACTER - ONE OF THE ASCII VALUES WHICH FILL THE LINE BUFFER.  THE
8481               /     POSSIBLE CHARACTERS ARE BACK SPACE, TAB, SPACE, AND TEXT.  THE
8482               /     LAST POSITION IN THE LINE BUFFER IS FILLED BY A RETURN, WHICH IS
8483               /     NOT A CHARACTER.
8484               
8485               /DEAD KEY SEQUENCE - A SEQUENCE OF TEXT DELIMITED BY BACK SPACES
8486               /     (I.E., TEXT1 BS TEXT2 BS TEXT3).  SUCH SEQUENCES ARE PRINTED WITH
8487               /     THE CHARACTERS SUPERIMPOSED.
8488               
8489               /POSITION - ALL THE CHARACTERS WHICH MAP TO THE SAME PHYSICAL PLACE ON
8490               /     THE PRINTED PAGE ARE SAID TO BE THE SAME POSITION.  THEREFORE,
8491               /     ALL THE CHARACTERS IN A DEAD KEY SEQUENCE ARE A POSITION.  A CHARACTER
8492               /     WHICH IS NOT PART OF A DEAD KEY SEQUENCE IS A POSITION.  IN THIS
8493               /     CODE, WE JUSTIFY BY POSITIONS; WE FIND THE WIDTH OF POSITIONS.  IT
8494               /     IS AN IMPORTANT CONCEPT.
8495               
8496               /WIDTH - THE SPACE OCCUPIED BY A POSITION WHEN IT IS PRINTED.  IN
8497               /     NON-PROPORTIONAL PRINTING, THE WIDTH IS STANDARD (PLNRCS).  IN
8498               /     PROPORTIONAL PRINTING, THE WIDTH VARIES DEPENDING ON THE CHARACTERS
8499               /     IN THE POSITION.
8500               
8501               /TEXT - ANY PRINTABLE ASCII CHARACTER
8502               
8503               
8504               /WE ALSO MAKE SOME ASSUMPTIONS:
8505               
8506               /1.  THE ONLY CHARACTERS IN THE BUFFER ARE RETURN, BACK SPACE, TAB, SPACE,
8507               /    AND TEXT.
8508               
8509               /2.  THE ONLY PLACE BACK SPACES OCCUR ARE BETWEEN TEXT.
8510               
8511               / THIS OVERLAY IS USED FOR MATRIX PRINTERS AND DD HOST                  /A211
8512               /PLPTR currently addresses the return word in the buffer.  Bit 1 of this word
8513               /is clear for a hard return and is set otherwise.  We save the type of the
8514               /return for later use.
8515               
8516                       AC2000                  /GET A MASK FOR THE SOFT RETURN BIT
undefined       	     ^
     030201* 0000  
8517 030202* 0436          AND I   PLPTR           /SEE IF SOFT RETURN
8518 030203* 3045          DCA     PRJRET          /RECORD THE TYPE OF RETURN.
8519                                               /PRJRET=2000 FOR SOFT RETURN
8520                                               /PRJRET=0000 FOR HARD,CENTERING, OR PARA MARKER
8521               
8522                       AC0001                  / INSURE PROPORTIONAL PRINTING OFF      /A219
undefined       	     ^
     030204* 0000  
8523 030205* 3000          DCA     PLPFLG          / PROPORTIONAL PRINTING OFF--OVJUSD     /A219
8524               
8525                                                                                       /A080
8526 030206* 3044          DCA     PLBOLD  /Reset SP PROPORTIONAL LQP02 flag.              /A086
8527               
8528               /We now set up some variables in order to process the line.  We want the
8529               /following conditions to hold:
8530               
8531               /PLPTR - Points to the return character (this already holds)
8532               
8533               /PLCNT - Is the negative of the number of characters, including the return,
8534               /               in the line.
8535               
8536               /PLDIR - Is minus one so that processing can proceed from right to left.
8537               
8538               PRJD0A,                                                         /A211
8539 030207* 1036          TAD     PLPTR   /Subtract the address of the return, and one more
8540 030210* 7040          CMA
