8792               /IN ORDER TO FACILITATE THE MULTIPLE PASS STRATEGY, THE MODE BITS OF
8793               /EACH CHARACTER MUST BE REARRANGED.  UPON CALL, THE MODE BITS OF EACH
8794               /CHARACTER ARE:
8795               
8796               /AC  2  3                       AC  4
8797               /    0  0   NORMAL                  0     NOT BOLD
8798               /    0  1   UNDERSCORE              1     BOLD
8799               /    1  0   SUPERSCRIPTED
8800               /    1  1   SUBSCRIPT
8801               
8802               
8803               /THE MODE SETTINGS WHICH THIS CODE UNDERSTANDS ARE:
8804               
8805               /AC  0
8806               /    0   THIS CHARACTER IS NOT A SPACE
8807               /    1   THIS CHARACTER IS A REAL SPACE THAT IS JUSTIFIABLE
8808               
8809               /AC  1  2
8810               /    0  0   ONE HIT (NORMAL TEXT)
8811               /    0  1   TWO HITS (NON-BOLDED, EXTRA DARK TEXT)
8812               /    1  0   THREE HITS (BOLDED, NON-EXTRA DARK TEXT)
8813               /    1  1   FOUR HITS (BOLDED, EXTRA DARK TEXT)
8814               
8815               /NOTICE THAT, IN ESSENCE, AC1 IS THE BOLD BIT AND AC2 IS THE DARKNESS BIT.
8816               /THE COMBINATION OF AC1 AND AC2 ARE CALLED THE HIT BITS; TAKEN TOGETHER,
8817               /THEY INDICATED ONE LESS THAN THE NUMBER OF PASSES IN WHICH A CHARACTER
8818               /SHOULD BE PRINTED TO OBTAIN THE DESIRED BOLDNESS/DARKNESS.
8819               
8820               
8821               /THE COMBINATIONS OF AC BITS 3 AND 4 ARE FOR UNDERLINING, SUPERSCRIPTING,
8822               /AND SUBSCRIPTING. THE COMBINATIONS ARE AS FOLLOWS;
8823               /AC  3  4
8824               /    0  0   NO SUBSCRIPT/SUPERSCRIPT, OR UNDERLINING.
8825               /    0  1   UNDERLINE
8826               /    1  0   SUPERSCRIPT
8827               /    1  1   SUBSCRIPT
