10257               
10258               /THIS OVERLAY IS RESPONSIBLE FOR JUSTIFYING (IF NECESSARY) AND PRINTING
10259               /THE LINE OF TEXT WHICH HAS BEEN ASSEMBLED IN PRLBUF BY PRGTLN
10260               /EXTERNAL ARGUMENT USED BY JUSTIFICATION OVERLAYS:
10261               
10262               /PLPTR - A POINTER INTO THE LINE BUFFER.  INITIALLY, IT POINTS AT THE LAST
10263               /         CHARACTER IN THE LINE, WHICH IS THE RETURN.
10264               
10265               /PRLBUF - A LITERAL WHICH IS THE ADDRESS OF THE BEGINNING OF THE BUFFER; IT
10266               /         IS THE ADDRESS AT WHICH THE FIRST CHARACTER IS STORED.
10267               
10268               /PRQPIT - THE PITCH VALUE.  IT IS ZERO IF PROPORTIONAL PITCH IS SPECIFIED,
10269               /         NON-ZERO OTHERWISE.
10270               
10271               /PRRM   - THE JUSTIFICATION FLAG.  IT IS ZERO IF THE LINE IS NOT TO BE
10272               /         JUSTIFIED; OTHERWISE, IT THE LENGTH OF THE LINE IN PRINT UNITS.
10273               
10274               /PLNRCS - CHARACTER SIZE.  IT IS THE SIZE OF A CHARACTER IN PRINT UNITS.
10275               
10276               /PRCCH  - PRINT HEAD POSITION.  INITIALLY, IT IS THE POSITION THE PRINT
10277               /         HEAD IS IN.
10278               /SOME DEFINITIONS WILL MAKE THE COMMENTS EASIER TO FOLLOW:
10279               
10280               /CHARACTER - ONE OF THE ASCII VALUES WHICH FILL THE LINE BUFFER.  THE
10281               /     POSSIBLE CHARACTERS ARE BACK SPACE, TAB, SPACE, AND TEXT.  THE
10282               /     LAST POSITION IN THE LINE BUFFER IS FILLED BY A RETURN, WHICH IS
10283               /     NOT A CHARACTER.
10284               
10285               /DEAD KEY SEQUENCE - A SEQUENCE OF TEXT DELIMITED BY BACK SPACES
10286               /     (I.E., TEXT1 BS TEXT2 BS TEXT3).  SUCH SEQUENCES ARE PRINTED WITH
10287               /     THE CHARACTERS SUPERIMPOSED.
10288               
10289               /POSITION - ALL THE CHARACTERS WHICH MAP TO THE SAME PHYSICAL PLACE ON
10290               /     THE PRINTED PAGE ARE SAID TO BE THE SAME POSITION.  THEREFORE,
10291               /     ALL THE CHARACTERS IN A DEAD KEY SEQUENCE ARE A POSITION.  A CHARACTER
10292               /     WHICH IS NOT PART OF A DEAD KEY SEQUENCE IS A POSITION.  IN THIS
10293               /     CODE, WE JUSTIFY BY POSITIONS; WE FIND THE WIDTH OF POSITIONS.  IT
10294               /     IS AN IMPORTANT CONCEPT.
10295               
10296               /WIDTH - THE SPACE OCCUPIED BY A POSITION WHEN IT IS PRINTED.  IN
10297               /     NON-PROPORTIONAL PRINTING, THE WIDTH IS STANDARD (PLNRCS).  IN
10298               /     PROPORTIONAL PRINTING, THE WIDTH VARIES DEPENDING ON THE CHARACTERS
10299               /     IN THE POSITION.
10300               
10301               /TEXT - ANY PRINTABLE ASCII CHARACTER
10302               
10303               
10304               /WE ALSO MAKE SOME ASSUMPTIONS:
10305               
10306               /1.  THE ONLY CHARACTERS IN THE BUFFER ARE RETURN, BACK SPACE, TAB, SPACE,
10307               /    AND TEXT.
10308               
10309               /2.  THE ONLY PLACE BACK SPACES OCCUR ARE BETWEEN TEXT.
10310               
