10717               
10718               /NOW WE SEE IF ANY JUSTIFICATION IS NECESSARY.  ALL SPACES IN THE
10719               /JUSTIFIABLE PORTION OF THE LINE ARE MARKED WITH BIT 0 SET.  AN EXTRA
10720               /PLSS UNITS ARE ADDED TO EACH SUCH SPACE.  IN ADDITION, PLSSC IS
10721               /INCREMENTED EACH TIME.  AS LONG AS IT REMAINS NEGATIVE OR ZERO, AN
10722               /EXTRA UNIT IS ADDED TO EACH SPACE.  SINCE ONLY UNITS IN MULTIPLES OF
10723               /SPACES ARE OUTPUT IN LPMOVE, LEFTOVER UNITS ARE RETAINED UNTIL THE
10724               /NEXT SPACE.
10725                       
10726               /FIRST DETERMINE IF THE CHARACTER JUST OUTPUT WAS A JUSTIFIABLE SPACE.
10727               
10728 030705* 1436          TAD I   PLPTR   /GET THE CHARACTER
10729 030706* 0356          AND     (4177   /MASK LEAVING ONLY JUSTIFICATION BIT AND CHR
10730 030707* 1355          TAD     (-4040) /SEE IF WAS A JUSTIFIABLE SPACE
10731 030710* 7640          SZA CLA         /SKIP IF SO
10732 030711* 5323          JMP     LNLIN8  /IT WASN'T--NO JUSTIFICATION
10733               
10734 030712* 1436          TAD I   PLPTR   /GET THE JUSTIFIABLE SPACE CODE
10735 030713* 7421          MQL             /AND PUT IN MQ FOR LPMOVE
10736               
10737               /Next determine how much space to add.  We increment PLSSC each time.  As soon
10738               /as it reaches zero, we now longer use one additional unit.
10739               
10740 030714* 2754          ISZ     PLSSC   /Increment the remainder counter
10741 030715* 7000          NOP             /In case it skips
10742               
10743 030716* 1754          TAD     PLSSC   /See if the remainder counter is still negative
10744 030717* 7710          SPA CLA
10745                       AC0001          /Yes--use one additional unit
undefined       	     ^
     030720* 0000  
10746               
10747 030721* 1000          TAD     PLSS    /Recover the extra space sizing
10748               
10749               /WE NOW HAVE THE AMOUNT OF EXTRA SPACING REQUIRED IN THE AC.  LPMOVE PADS
10750               /OUT AS MUCH OF THE EXTRA SPACE AS IT CAN BY PRINTING THE CHARACTER IN THE
10751               /MQ.
10752               
10753 030722* 4753          JMS     LPMOVE  /DO THE MOTION
10754               
10755 030723* 4752  LNLIN8, JMS     PLNXT   /POINT AT THE NEXT CHARACTER
10756 030724* 5334          JMP     LNLI11  /NO MORE CHARACTERS--END OF THE LINE
10757 030725* 1436          TAD I   PLPTR   /GET THE NEXT CHARACTER
10758 030726* 1351          TAD     (-BS)   /IS IT A BACKSPACE?
10759 030727* 7640          SZA CLA
10760 030730* 5201          JMP     LNLIN3  /NO--THIS IS A DESIRED CHARACTER
10761               
10762               /WE HAVE FOUND A BACKSPACE; OUTPUT IT & DO NEXT CHR.
10763               
10764 030731* 1436          TAD I   PLPTR
10765 030732* 4763          JMS     PRCHAR
10766 030733* 5323          JMP     LNLIN8
10767               
10768               
10769               /WE ARE THROUGH WITH THE LINE.  WE MUST MAKE SURE THE
10770               /CARRIAGE IS RETURNED TO THE PROPER VERICAL POSITION
10771               /AND THAT BOLDING/UNDERLINING ARE OFF
10772               
10773 030734* 4777  LNLI11, JMS     PRMODE  /CALL ROUTINE TO CLEAR SUPER/SUB UNDL/BOLD
10774 030735* 1350          TAD     (CR)    /SEND A CARRIAGE RETURN TO END THE LINE
10775 030736* 4763          JMS     PRCHAR
10776 030737* 5747          JMP     PRGSL1  /ENTER THE SPACING ROUTINE. IT IS END OF PRINT LINE.
