10780               /THIS ROUTINE IS USED TO SEND OUT THE ESCAPE SEQUENCES TO SET UP THE
10781               /PROPER VERTICAL POSITION, BOLD ATTRIBUTE, AND UNDERLINE ATTRIBUTE.
10782               /IT USES ANSI SEQUENCES TO DO THIS (PLU, PLD AND SGR).  PRINTERS WHICH
10783               /CAN ACCEPT THESE SEQUENCES DO NOT NEED A MULTIPLE PASS STRATEGY TO PRINT
10784               /THE LINE.
10785               
10786               /ORIGINALLY ADDED FOR THE "LN03 DRIVER"                         /A247
10787               
10788               /IT HAS THE SAME NAME AS PRMODE SO IT CAN USE THE SAME VERT ROUTINE
10789               
10790               /NOW THAT WE ARE SUPPORTING A PRINTER THAT HAS MULTIPLE FONT CAPABILITY,
10791               /WE FIND THAT THE OLDS WAYS ARE NOT ADEQUATE.  PLU AND PLD ARE DEFINED
10792               /TO BE HALF A LINE UP OR DOWN BASED ON THE CURRENT VERTICAL SPACING,
10793               /WHICH IS CALCULATED FROM THE FONT.  THUS IF WE CHANGE FONTS IN THE
10794               /MIDDLE OF A LINE USING BOLD INTERPRETATION, AND THE NEW FONT HAS A
10795               /DIFFERENT SIZE THAN THE OLD FONT, WE MUST BE CAREFUL ABOUT THE ORDER
10796               /IN WHICH WE DO THINGS, ELSE WE MAY INDUCE A BASELINE SHIFT WHEN GOING
10797               /FROM BOLDED SUPERS TO NON BOLDED NORMAL TEXT OR VICE VERSA.
10798               
10799               /THUS WE ESTABLISH THE FOLLOWING RULE:
10800               /  1.   WHEN GOING FROM A NONBOLDED BASELINE TO A BOLDED SUPER OR SUB,
10801               /       DO THE FONT CHANGE AFTER THE VERTICAL MOTION.
10802               /  2.   WHEN GOING FROM A BOLDED SUPER OR SUB TO A NONBOLDED CHR
10803               /       IN A DIFFERENT VERTICAL POSITION, DO THE FONT CHANGE BEFORE
10804               /       THE VERTICAL MOTION
10805               
10806               PRMODE, XX
