12852               DCSESC="/&177           /CHARACTER TO CHANGE MODES                      /A257
12853               
12854               / WE NOW ENTER THE OCTAL NUMERIC MODE.  IF AND/OR WHEN WE ENCOUNTER
12855               / A DCSESC CHARACTER, WE WILL ENTER THE TEXT MODE.  WE WILL STAY IN THE TEXT
12856               / MODE UNTIL WE ENCOUNTER ANOTHER DCSESC CHARACTER, WHICH WILL PUT US BACK IN
12857               / THE OCTAL NUMERIC MODE, ETC. UNTIL THE END OF THE LINE
12858               
12859               / WE CONVERT NUMERIC CHARACTERS ON THE FLY, BUT IF WE ENCOUNTER
12860               / TEXT WE WILL BUFFER IT IN THE TOKEN BUFFER UNTIL A SEPARATOR IS FOUND.
12861               / WE THEN SEE IF THE TOKEN IS THE NAME OF AN ASCII CHARACTER.  IF SO,
12862               / WE TRANSMIT THE APPROPRIATE ASCII VALUE.  IF THE TEXT IS NOT MATCHED
12863               / WE ENTER THE TEXT MODE SO THE USER CAN SEE THE MISTAKE.
12864               
12865               / AT THE END OF THE LINE WE RETURN TO PARSE ANY CONTROLS WHICH
12866               / MAY COME AFTER PRINTER.  END OF LINE HAS NO EFFECT IN TEXT MODE
12867               
12868               / IN THE NUMERIC MODE WE TREAT THE SPACE CHARACTER AS A SEPARATOR
12869               / BETWEEN SUCESSIVE NUMERIC CHARACTERS.  A SPACE IS NOT REQUIRED
12870               / BEFORE A DCSESC CHARACTER MODE CHANGE CHARACTER.
12871               
