13457               
13458               /THIS SECTION HANDLES PAGE FORMATTING.  THE PAGE CAN BE DIVIDED INTO SEVEN
13459               /SECTIONS, AND THIS OVERLAY IS DIVIDED INTO SEVEN SECTIONS TO HANDLE THESE
13460               /DIVISIONS.  THE SEVEN SECTIONS, THE ASSUMPTIONS OF EACH, AND THE ACTIONS
13461               /OF EACH ARE DETAILED BELOW:
13462               
13463               /TOP OF HEADER (TOPH)
13464               
13465               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED AT THE TOP PAGE BOUNDARY.
13466               
13467               /ACTION - IF A HEADER IS NOT IN EFFECT, THE PAGE IS MOVED TO THE BEGINNING
13468               /         OF THE TEXT AREA (FOLLOWING THE TOP MARGIN) AND WE CONTINUE WITH
13469               /         NEW COLUMNS.  IF A HEADER IS IN EFFECT, THE PAGE IS MOVED TO
13470               /         THE BEGINNING OF THE HEADER AREA.  PREPARATION IS THEN MADE
13471               /         TO PRINT THE HEADER AND WE CONTINUE WITH MORE SPACING.
13472               
13473               
13474               /BOTTOM OF HEADER (BOTH)
13475               
13476               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED SOMEWHERE IN THE TOP MARGIN AREA.
13477               
13478               /ACTION - THE PAGE IS MOVED TO THE BEGINNING OF THE TEXT AREA (FOLLOWING
13479               /         THE TOP MARGIN.  PREPARATION IS MADE TO RESTORE REGULAR TEXT
13480               /         PRINTING.  WE CONTINUE WITH NEW COLUMNS.
13481               
13482               
13483               /NEW COLUMNS (NEWC)
13484               
13485               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED AT THE BEGINNING OF THE COLUMN AREA.
13486               /              THIS CAN BE ANYWHERE ON THE PAGE BELOW THE TOP MARGIN, SINCE
13487               /              A NEW SET OF COLUMNS CAN BEGIN ANYWHERE.
13488               
13489               /ACTION - THE COLUMN VARIABLES ARE INITIALIZED AND WE CONTINUE WITH MORE
13490               /         SPACING.
13491               
13492               
13493               /NEXT COLUMN (NXTC)
13494               
13495               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED ANYWHERE BELOW THE TOP MARGIN.
13496               
13497               /ACTION - IF ANOTHER COLUMN IS TO BE PRINTED, THE PAGE IS POSITIONED TO
13498               /         BEGIN THE NEW COLUMN AND WE CONTINUE WITH MORE SPACING.  IF
13499               /         ALL THE COLUMNS HAVE BEEN PRINTED, WE CONTINUE WITH TOP OF
13500               /         FOOTER.
13501               
13502               
13503               /TOP OF FOOTER (TOPF)
13504               
13505               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED ANYWHERE BELOW THE TOP MARGIN.
13506               
13507               /ACTION - NORMAL INDENTATION IS RESTORED AND THE PAGE IS MOVED TO THE
13508               /         BEGINNING OF THE BOTTOM MARGIN OR TO THE END OF THE LONGEST
13509               /         COLUMN, WHICHEVER IS GREATER.  IF THERE IS A FOOTER IN EFFECT
13510               /         AND ROOM TO PRINT IT, FOOTER PRINTING IS SET UP AND WE CONTINUE
13511               /         WITH MORE SPACING.  OTHERWISE, WE CONTINUE WITH BOTTOM OF PAGE.
13512               
13513               
13514               /BOTTOM OF FOOTER (BOTF)
13515               
13516               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED SOMEWHERE IN THE BOTTOM MARGIN.
13517               
13518               /ACTION - NORMAL TEXT PRINTING IS RESTORED AND WE CONTINUE WITH BOTTOM
13519               /         OF PAGE.
13520               
13521               
13522               /BOTTOM OF PAGE (BOTP)
13523               
13524               /ASSUMPTIONS - THE PAGE IS POSITIONED ANYWHERE.
13525               
13526               /ACTION - THE PAGE NUMBER IS INCREMENTED AND THE PAGE IS MOVED TO THE
13527               /         NEXT PAGE BOUNDARY.  IF WE ARE AT THE END OF THE FILE, PRINTING
13528               /         OF THE CURRENT COPY IS TERMINATED.  OTHERWISE, WE CONTINUE WITH
13529               /         TOP OF PAGE PROCESSING.       
13530               
13531               
13532               
13533               /THIS SECTION HANDLES THE TOP OF THE HEADER.
13534               
13535               OVTOPH=.-OVRLCA
13536               OBTOPH=OVTYPE+OVNUM
13537               
13538               /IF PRINTING IS CURRENTLY SUPPRESSED, THERE IS NO NEED TO PROCESS A HEADER.
13539               
13540 040601* 1034          TAD     PRYES   /IS PRINTING INHIBITED?
13541 040602* 7640          SZA CLA
13542 040603* 5207          JMP     TOPHL0  /YES--DO NOT PRINT THE HEADER
13543               
13544               /DETERMINE WHETHER OR NOT A HEADER IS IN EFFECT.
13545               
13546 040604* 1051          TAD     PRHSIZ  /GET THE HEADER SIZE.  IF NON-ZERO, THERE IS A HEADER.
13547 040605* 7440          SZA
13548 040606* 5212          JMP     TOPHL1  /THERE IS A HEADER--JUMP TO HANDLE IT
13549               
13550               /THERE IS NO HEADER--SPACE THE TOP MARGIN AND CONTINUE WITH NEW COLUMNS.
13551               
13552               TOPHL0,
13553 040607* 1777          TAD     PRQTMG  /GET THE TOP MARGIN
13554 040610* 4776          JMS     PRMOVE  /MOVE IT
13555 040611* 5241          JMP     PRNEWC  /CONTINUE WITH NEW COLUMNS
13556               
13557               /THERE IS A HEADER IN EFFECT--PREPARE TO PRINT IT.
