13727               
13728               /THIS SECTION HANDLES TOP OF FOOTER PROCESSING.
13729               
13730               / IN PREVIOUS VERSIONS, FOOTERS WERE ALLOWED TO FLOAT DOWNWARD IF THE
13731               / BOTTOM MARGIN WAS INVADED BY EXTRA LINES (THIS CAN ONLY HAPPEN IN APNO).
13732               / AS OF THIS REWRITE (REV161) THE FOOTER POSITION WILL ALWAYS BE FIXED.
13733               / IF THE BOTTOM MARGIN IS INVADED, LINES WILL BE STRIPPED FROM THE TOP
13734               / OF THE FOTTER EVEN THOUGH THE FOOTER SIZE MAY BE LESS THAN THE BOTTOM
13735               / MARGIN SIZE.  THE CLEVER WPS USER WHO WANTS TO USE GOLD PAGE AND VIEW
13736               / ORPHAN LINES, AND DISCRETIONALLY MOVE DOWN THE NEW PAGE MARKER TO
13737               / ELIMINATE THEM, WILL LEAVE SOME BLANK LINES AT THE TOP OF THE FOOTER
13738               / TO FACILITATE HIS DESIRE.
13739               
13740               / THE PREVIOUS METHOD (REV161), IN REPOSITIONING TO THE TOP OF THE      /A200
13741               / FOOTER, REQUIRED REVERSE MOTION, IF THE NEXT HAD INVADED THE FOOTER.  /A200
13742               / THIS CAUSED A BUG ON DRAFT PRINTERS WHICH ARE NOT PROGRAMMED TO       /A200
13743               / DO REVERSE MOTION.  THUS, ALL REVERSE MOTION TO DRAFT PRINTER WAS     /A200
13744               / IGNORED AND THE PAGE REFERENCE WAS LOST                               /A200
13745               / NOW (REV200) WE WILL NOT DO ANY REVERSE MOTION, SINCE NONE            /A200
13746               / IS REALLY NECESSARY, BUT WE MUST CHANGE OUR ALGORITHM A LITTLE        /A200
13747               
13748               PRTOPF,
13749 041000* 3046          DCA     PRMCPC  /SHOW NO COLUMN PRINTING
