14811               
14812               /THIS OVERLAY HANDLES THE PROCESSING WHEN THE PRINTER IS STOPPED.  THERE ARE
14813               /MANY REASONS WHY THE PRINTER CAN BE STOPPED.  THESE REASONS, ALONG WITH THE
14814               /CODE IDENTIFYING THE REASON IN PRSTTS, ARE:
14815               
14816               / 2 - THE USER REQUESTED THAT THE PRINTER STOP
14817               / 3 - STOPPED AT THE TOP OF A PAGE FOR "SE FIRST"
14818               / 4 - STOPPED AT THE TOP OF A PAGE FOR "SE YES"
14819               / 5 - STOPPED AT THE END OF A PAGE BECAUSE THE USER REQESTED THAT THE
14820               /      PRINTER STOP AT THE END OF THE NEXT PAGE
14821               / 6 - STOPPED AT THE END OF A COPY BECAUSE TWO-WHEEL PROCESSING WAS IN
14822               /      EFFECT AND IT IS TIME FOR THE PRINT WHEEL CHANGE
14823               / 7 - STOPPED BECAUSE THE DOCUMENT DESTINATION SPECIFIED BY THE USER IS
14824               /      A NON-EXISTENT PRINTER
14825               /10 - THE DOCUMENT DESTINATION DOES NOT MATCH THE ATTACHED PRINTER
14826               /11 - PRTID RECEIVED AN ID BUT NO XON.  WE PRESUME THE PAUSE SWITCH
14827               /       WAS ON.
14828               /12 - STOPPED BECAUSE THE DOCUMENT DESTINATION SPECIFIED BY THE USER
14829               /      REQUIRES THE USE OF A COMMUNICATION LINE WHICH IS ALREADY IN USE.
14830               /13 - STOPPED BECAUSE OF A MALFUNCTION (FATAL ERROR).
14831               /15 - THE PAUSE SWITCH IS ON
14832               /16 - OUT OF RIBBON
14833               /17 - SHEET FEEDER ERROR--LQP02
14834               /20 - COVER OPEN
14835               /21 - OUT OF PAPER
14836               /22 - DOCUMENT DISK READ ERROR
14837               /23 - SYSTEM DISK READ ERROR
14838               /24 - SHEET FEEDER ERROR--LQPSE
14839               /25 - LQPSE FATAL ERROR (CANCEL)
14840               /26 - COMMUNICATIONS ERROR TO PRINTER                                   /A155
14841               
14842               /THE USER HAS SEVERAL ACTION OPTIONS OPEN DEPENDING ON WHAT TYPE OF STOP
14843               /WE HAVE.  ONE OR MORE OF THE FOLLOWING ACTIONS MAY BE ALLOWED DEPENDING
14844               /ON THE STOP REASON.  WHICH ACTIONS ARE ALLOWED IS DETERMINED BY A TABLE
14845               /IN WPCUT.
14846               
14847               /-1. LIST THE DOCUMENTS IN THE PRINT QUEUE
14848               /1.  MOVE THE PAPER TO THE NEXT PAGE BOUNDARY
14849               /2.  ABORT PRINTING THE DOCUMENT
14850               /3.  CONTINUE PRINTING TIL THE END OF THE PAGE
14851               /4.  RESTART FROM THE BEGINNING OF THE CURRENT COPY
14852               /5.  GO BACK N PAGES AND RESTART
14853               /6.  CONTINUE PRINTING
14854               /7.  CHANGE DOCUMENT DESTINATION (RESPONSE TO CODE 10 ONLY)
14855               
14856               /THIS IS THE ENTRY POINT IF THE PRINTER IS STOPPED DUE TO USER REQUEST
14857               /OR A CUT SHEET FEEDER ERROR.  IF AN ASF IS ATTACHED NO PAPER WILL BE
14858               /FED AFTER A P OR R RESPONSE.
14859               
