15127               /                                                               /A154
15128               / HERE WE USED TO (REV056 TO REV153) SEE IF THERE WAS ANOTHER ERROR
15129               / AS FOUND IN PRSTT2.  IF SO, WE WOULD COPY THAT TO PRSTTS AND
15130               / RE-DO THE STOP.
15131               
15132               / THE NEW WAY THAT 2ND ERRORS ARE HANDLED IS AS FOLLOWS.  THE OPERATOR
15133               / MAKES A DECISION ON HOW TO HANDLE AN ERROR WHEN HE/SHE IS IN THE STOP
15134               / MENU.  THE PRRSST ROUTINE DECIDES ON WHETHER THE USER OR PRINTER WILL
15135               / RESET THAT STATUS ERROR.  WHEN IT IS RESET, A SECOND ERROR WILL BE
15136               / COPIED UP AND ANOTHER PRINTER STOPPED MESSAGE WILL BE RECEIVED, AND
15137               / THAT ERROR WILL BE HANDLED ON ITS OWN MERITS.
15138               
15139               / CAUTION: WPCUT SENDS TO THE STOP MENU A BIT MASK WHICH SELECTIVELY
15140               / ENABLES THE OPTIONS THAT THE OPERATOR SEES.
15141               /                                                               /A154
15142               /***************************************************************/A154
